# Feature: Production release & ERP integration

## Flow
Final approval + costing complete → `PRODUCTION_RELEASED` →
1) In-app ERP chain stages seeded (Grey→…→Accounts) — operate at `/production/erp`
2) Outbound partner handoffs: Grey/Material → Cutting → Embroidery → Garmenting → Finishing → Ready Stock
→ Sales → Sales Return → Accounts/GST/TDS → feeds Design Success KPI.

See `Docs/ERP_DOWNSTREAM_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md` and `Docs/ERP_DOWNSTREAM_E2E_UPDATE.md`.

## Rules
- Validate mandatory approvals + mandatory costing/files before marking a
  design released - this check happens server-side, not just in the UI.
- After release, the design reference must be available to existing
  production transactions for traceability.
- Design-success KPI consumes downstream production, sales, sales-return and
  margin data joined by Design Number/SKU (in-app stages update metrics on complete).
- Production Head can view approved designs and accept release but cannot
  alter prior design history.
- Handoff modules: `ERP_HANDOFF_MODULES` (includes `SALES_RETURN`).
  In-app `ErpStageRecord` is the operational chain; partner POST remains optional live sync.
